---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Changelog - Fomawrite" description="Development history and release notes for Fomawrite">
  <Nav />
  
  <main>
    <div class="container">
      <header class="page-header">
        <h1>Changelog</h1>
        <p>Development history and release notes. Latest cycles first.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="changelog">
        <section class="changelog-section">
          <h2>0.3.0 Development Series</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">Current focus: making Live editing good enough to be the daily editor</p>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 151</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev47 · Build 151 · Oct 12, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <p>Folder back/forward arrows in the middle pane and ⌘↑ for the enclosing folder there.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 150</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev46 · Build 150 · Oct 12, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <p>The folder chooser opens inside the current folder (build 149 started it one level up).</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 149</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev45 · Build 149 · Oct 12, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <p>The folder chooser starts where the folder lives: opens in the folder that holds the current one, with that folder selected, instead of at the top of the disk.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 148</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev44 · Build 148 · Oct 12, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <p>Getting from the open document to its folder: the top-bar document name shows the full path on hover and opens the file menu on right-click. New Explore Folder item makes the file's folder the middle pane's folder with the file selected.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 147</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev43 · Build 147 · Oct 11, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <p>Harper in daily use: Live underlines long lists of misspellings (the host lints pages line by line). A suggestion in the Review pane removes its row at once and selects the next. The missing-theme-font notice is a one-time banner.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 146</h3>
              <span class="version">Build 146 · Oct 11, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <p>Keeping Harper current: Help → Check for Writing Checker Updates downloads the newest harper.js from npm. Weekly automatic checks (switchable). Help → Use Built-in Writing Checker rolls back.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 145</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev41 · Build 145 · Oct 11, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <p>Harper: Automattic's offline grammar engine runs inside the editor page. Third category Style (grey). Edit → Writing Checker: Engine (Harper / macOS), Dialect (Australian, British, American, Canadian). Claude Like theme reworked to match the Claude Code output page.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 144</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev40 · Build 144 · Oct 10, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <p>Grammar as you type and the Review pane: the shared checker gains grammar findings. Source draws them as blue underline with wash, Live as wavy blue underline. Modal Spelling and Grammar dialog is gone; new resizable Review pane lists every finding with sentence, category, message, suggestions.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 143</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev39 · Build 143 · Oct 10, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <p>Spelling as you type in Source and Live: misspelled prose gets red underline from one shared system checker, skipping code, links, URLs, HTML, math, front matter. Right-click offers suggestions, Learn Spelling, Ignore Spelling.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 134</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev30 · Build 134 · Oct 6-7, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <p><strong>The Live editor:</strong> CodeMirror 6 editor page hosted in the app's WebEngineView over QWebChannel. Byte-exact two-way mirror with the canonical document. Live mode (inline marks, images, tasks, rules, highlighted fences, table grids, KaTeX math). Source/Code appearances with focus and typewriter. Theme pass-through, scroll sync, cursor carry-over, Format/Undo/Find routed to the page. Image paste/drop saved beside the document. In-page link editor. 1 MiB document loads in ~55 ms.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 133</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev29 · Build 133</span>
            </div>
            <p>Structure, CI and measured hot path: GitHub Actions CI with pinned Qt 6.11.3. Publishing extracted into Publisher behind PublishingSource. Mapper O(n²) fixed (100 KB line 4.1 s → 0.7 ms). 220 tests.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 132</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev28 · Build 132</span>
            </div>
            <p>Publishing robustness: theme refresh compares catalog + selected CSS, memoized CSS and image cache, fingerprint cache key, shared Chromium profile, failures keep last output, renderer-crash handling. 212 tests.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Cycle 131</h3>
              <span class="version">0.3.0-dev27 · Build 131</span>
            </div>
            <p>Byte-exact persistence: raw-byte open with UTF-8 validation and UTF-16 BOM detection, lossy decodes block in-place Save, canonical text keeps NBSP/U+2028, CRLF/CR/BOM preserved, manual Save checks disk baseline. 208 tests.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="changelog-section">
          <h2>Earlier Series</h2>
          <p class="section-note">Full history in <a href="https://github.com/andrewjngray/fomawrite_mac/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CHANGELOG.md</a></p>
          
          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>0.2.x series</h3>
              <span class="version">Cycles 60–89</span>
            </div>
            <p>Workspace redesign, Visual Edit baseline, Export hub with PDF/HTML and style gallery, authorship annotations, recovery and versions, native tabs and coordination, focus tools, rich Markdown extensions.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Omawrite-era cycles</h3>
              <span class="version">Cycles 14–59</span>
            </div>
            <p>Menu and workflow implementation: Format menu, Go menu locations, View chrome, Library/List navigation, Templates, Locations and Favorites, File operations, Search and tags, Command palette, Publishing preview, Markdown editing commands, Find/Replace.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="changelog-item">
            <div class="item-header">
              <h3>Foundation</h3>
              <span class="version">Cycles 0–13</span>
            </div>
            <p>macOS foundation with native menus and dialogs, UTF-8 saving, explorer, editor, live preview, source markup, paragraph/typewriter focus, outline and statistics, organizer favorites and recents.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  main {
    min-height: calc(100vh - 64px);
    padding: var(--spacing-2xl) 0;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .page-header p {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .changelog {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }

  .changelog-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .section-intro,
  .section-note {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .changelog-item {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .changelog-item:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .item-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .item-header h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .version {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-dim);
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Code', 'Source Code Pro', Menlo, Consolas, 'DejaVu Sans Mono', monospace;
  }

  .changelog-item p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .item-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }
</style>
